lection\" style=\"width: 22.2843%;\">&nbsp;4.11-21.85</td>\n<td class=\"cke_table-faked-selection\" style=\"width: 43.3306%;\">&nbsp;</td>\n<td class=\"cke_table-faked-selection\" style=\"width: 21.9748%;\">&nbsp;</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"><strong>CLINICAL USE:</strong></span></p>\n<p><br><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">Evaluation of gonadal hormonal function.</span><br><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">&nbsp;</span><br><strong><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">DECREASED IN:</span></strong></p>\n<p><br><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">Primary hypogonadism (eg: orchiectomy)</span><br><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">Secondary hypogonadism (eg: hypopituitarism)</span><br><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">Testicular feminization.</span><br><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">Estrogen therapy</span><br><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">&nbsp;</span><br><strong><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">INCREASED IN:</span></strong><br><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">&nbsp;</span><br><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">Adrenal virilising tumor causing premature puberty in boys or masculinization in women</span><br><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">Congenital adrenal hyperplasia</span><br><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">Idiopathic hirsutism- inconclusive</span><br><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">Ovarian stromal hyperthecosis</span><br><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">&nbsp;</span><br><strong><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">NOTE:</span></strong><br><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">&nbsp;</span><br><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">The clinical significance of the determination of Free Testosterone can be invalidated if the patient was treated cortisone or natural synthetic steroids.</span></p>",
